<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4578] SQL: Statement cache can cause memory leak</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4578</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;We have prepared statement cache in IgniteH2Indexing declared as Map&amp;lt;Thread, StatementCache&amp;gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
This can cause memory leak if threads will die unexpetedly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We should declare StatementCache as ThreadLocal field. This along with separate thread pool for SQL queries (see &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4105&quot; title=&quot;Create separate thread pool for SQL queries&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-4105&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-4105&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) should resolve the issue..&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13036486">IGNITE-4578</key>
